# Inventory Management

A production-oriented inventory management application with a **.NET 8 ASP.NET Core Web API**, **React + TypeScript + Vite** frontend, **PostgreSQL**, **Clean Architecture**, **Vertical Slice Architecture**, **CQRS + MediatR**, **ASP.NET Identity**, **JWT Authentication**, **Refresh Token Rotation**, **Serilog**, and **Docker**.

The project supports multi-company inventory workflows, company-scoped authorization, company-isolated master data and transactions, invitation-based member access, and a SaaS-ready subscription foundation.

---

## Features

### Architecture

* Clean Architecture
* Vertical Slice Architecture
* CQRS with MediatR
* Repository Pattern
* Dependency Injection
* FluentValidation Pipeline Behavior

### Authentication & Authorization

* ASP.NET Identity
* JWT Authentication
* Refresh Token Rotation
* Company-scoped membership roles
* Policy-based Authorization
* Active company selection through `X-Company-Id`

### Inventory Workflows

* Multi-company registration, company selection, invitations, and member access
* Product, category, unit, supplier, customer, and driver management
* Company-scoped subscriptions with Free plan limit checks
* Stock ledger with damage, adjustment, and reversal movements
* Purchase draft, edit, post, and cancel lifecycle
* Delivery challan draft, edit, post, and cancel lifecycle
* Direct sales invoices and invoices created from posted challans
* Customer and supplier payments with payment reversals
* Customer and supplier returns
* Current stock, ledger, register, gross profit, and statement reports

### Logging & Error Handling

* Global Exception Middleware
* Structured Logging with Serilog
* Console and File Logging

### Database

* Entity Framework Core
* PostgreSQL
* Company-scoped indexes and constraints
* Case-insensitive uniqueness with PostgreSQL `citext`
* Automatic EF Core Migrations on Startup in Development

### DevOps

* Multi-stage Docker Build
* Docker Compose
* Persistent Database Volume
* Persistent Log Volume

---

## Workflow Rules

Documents are created as drafts where applicable. Drafts do not change stock or balances.

* Posting a purchase increases stock and updates weighted-average cost.
* Posting a delivery challan decreases stock without creating customer debt.
* Posting a direct sales invoice decreases stock and updates customer debt.
* Invoicing posted challans does not reduce stock a second time.
* Posting returns applies the corresponding stock and balance effects.
* Cancelling posted documents preserves history through reversal movements.
* Gross profit uses historical costs stored with sales and returns, not the product's current average cost.

---

## API Overview

Swagger provides complete request and response schemas. Authentication routes
and public invitation token routes do not require an active company. Most
business routes require a bearer access token and `X-Company-Id`; backend
authorization validates the caller's membership and role for that company.

### Authentication, Account, And Company

| Area | Routes |
| --- | --- |
| Authentication | `POST /api/Auth/Register`, `POST /api/Auth/Login`, `POST /api/Auth/RefreshToken` |
| Current user | `GET /api/Users/me`, `POST /api/Users/me/change-password` |
| Company access | `GET /api/companies`, `POST /api/companies`, `PUT /api/companies/{companyId}`, `GET /api/companies/current/access` |
| Members | `GET /api/Users`, `POST /api/Users/{userId}/roles`, `DELETE /api/Users/{userId}/roles/{role}`, `POST /api/Users/{userId}/disable`, `POST /api/Users/{userId}/enable` |
| Invitations | `GET /api/company-invitations`, `POST /api/company-invitations`, `DELETE /api/company-invitations/{id}`, `GET /api/company-invitations/{token}`, `POST /api/company-invitations/{token}/accept` |
| Company profile | `GET /api/company-profile`, `PUT /api/company-profile` |
| Subscription | `GET /api/subscription/current` |

### Master Data And Stock

| Area | Routes |
| --- | --- |
| Products | `GET/POST /api/products`, `GET/PUT/DELETE /api/products/{id}` |
| Product units | `GET/POST /api/products/{productId}/unit-conversions`, `PUT/PATCH /api/products/{productId}/unit-conversions/{id}` |
| Categories | `GET/POST /api/categories`, `GET/PUT/DELETE /api/categories/{id}` |
| Units | `GET/POST /api/units`, `GET/PUT/DELETE /api/units/{id}` |
| Customers | `GET/POST /api/customers`, `GET/PUT /api/customers/{id}`, `PATCH /api/customers/{id}/deactivate` |
| Suppliers | `GET/POST /api/suppliers`, `GET/PUT/DELETE /api/suppliers/{id}` |
| Drivers | `GET/POST /api/drivers`, `GET/PUT /api/drivers/{id}`, `PATCH /api/drivers/{id}/deactivate`, `GET /api/drivers/{id}/deliveries` |
| Stock movements | `GET /api/stock-movements`, `POST /api/stock-movements/damage`, `POST /api/stock-movements/adjustment`, `POST /api/stock-movements/{id}/reverse` |

### Transactions

| Area | Routes |
| --- | --- |
| Purchases | `GET/POST /api/purchases`, `GET/PUT /api/purchases/{id}`, `POST /api/purchases/{id}/post`, `POST /api/purchases/{id}/cancel` |
| Delivery challans | `GET/POST /api/delivery-challans`, `GET/PUT /api/delivery-challans/{id}`, `POST /api/delivery-challans/{id}/post`, `POST /api/delivery-challans/{id}/cancel`, `POST /api/delivery-challans/{id}/delivery-charge/mark-paid` |
| Sales invoices | `GET/POST /api/sales-invoices`, `POST /api/sales-invoices/from-challans`, `GET/PUT /api/sales-invoices/{id}`, `POST /api/sales-invoices/{id}/post`, `POST /api/sales-invoices/{id}/cancel`, `POST /api/sales-invoices/{id}/delivery-charge/mark-paid` |
| Payments | `GET /api/payments`, `POST /api/payments`, `POST /api/payments/{id}/reverse` |
| Customer returns | `GET /api/customer-returns/{id}`, `POST /api/customer-returns`, `POST /api/customer-returns/{id}/post`, `POST /api/customer-returns/{id}/cancel` |
| Supplier returns | `GET /api/supplier-returns/{id}`, `POST /api/supplier-returns`, `POST /api/supplier-returns/{id}/post`, `POST /api/supplier-returns/{id}/cancel` |

### Reports And Ledgers

| Route | Filters and result |
| --- | --- |
| `GET /api/inventory-reports/current-stock` | Paged stock by category, search text, and quantity filter |
| `GET /api/inventory-reports/products/{productId}/ledger` | Paged stock history by date and movement type |
| `GET /api/inventory-reports/purchase-register` | Purchases and summary by date, supplier, product, and status |
| `GET /api/inventory-reports/sales-register` | Sales and summary by date, customer, product, source, and status |
| `GET /api/inventory-reports/gross-profit` | Revenue, cost of goods sold, returns, and gross profit |
| `GET /api/customers/{id}/statement` | Customer ledger by date range |
| `GET /api/suppliers/{id}/statement` | Supplier ledger by date range |

Paged endpoints use `pageNumber` and `pageSize`. Report filters are applied
inside the active company scope.

---

## Architecture

```text
React/Vite SPA
    |
    | Bearer token + X-Company-Id
    v
ASP.NET Core API
    |
    +-- Controllers and authorization policies
    +-- MediatR feature handlers and FluentValidation
    +-- Application services for company access and subscription limits
    +-- EF Core repositories scoped by active company
    v
PostgreSQL
```

The backend follows Clean Architecture:

* `InventoryManagement.API` owns controllers, middleware, authentication,
  authorization policy registration, Swagger, CORS, rate limiting, and startup.
* `InventoryManagement.Application` owns CQRS requests, handlers, validators,
  DTOs, policy constants, and service abstractions.
* `InventoryManagement.Domain` owns entities and enums.
* `InventoryManagement.Infrastructure` owns EF Core, migrations, repositories,
  Identity, document numbering, company membership, default company data, and
  subscription-limit services.
* `InventoryManagement.Tests` contains unit and integration tests.
* `inventory-web` contains the React/TypeScript/Vite frontend.

Users can belong to multiple companies through `CompanyUser`. Business data,
document sequences, profile data, reports, and subscription-limited actions are
enforced on the backend; frontend route hiding is not relied on for security.

